title    Seven Eighths Fusion (swung seven)
composer Claude
about    Revision of the 4-bar 7/8 fusion loop. Same chords, voicings, instruments, bar length and tempo, but the groove is re-felt as a swung jazz-trio seven in the spirit of Brad Mehldau's All the Things You Are, phrased 2+2+3.

# Revision note. Feedback: "fusion 7 feels lame. keep everything, just make
# the groove like mehldau all the things we are 7 feel".
# Reading: Mehldau's trio plays All the Things You Are in a fast, swinging
# seven with quarter-note pulse: walking bass, ride cymbal time, hi-hat foot,
# and comping that floats over the bar line. The original was a straight
# sixteenth fusion groove with a kick/snare backbeat and stabs locked to the
# group starts, which is what read as "lame".
# What stays: harmony (Dm11, Bbmaj13#11, Gm9, Gm9 -> A7alt), every keys and
# pad voicing, the instruments, the 2+2+3 grouping, the bar length and the
# tempo number.
# What changes: the 240 pulse is now felt as swung quarters (a fast 7/4,
# close to the reference tempo) instead of straight eighths subdivided into
# straight sixteenths. Each step is now a swung eighth, so the notation grid
# and bar length are unchanged and only the feel moves.
tempo    240
beats    7
steps    2
# Swing added: fast swing flattens toward even eighths, so this is moderate.
swing    0.28

# Keys: same rootless voicings, now comped sparsely on swung upbeats with
# anticipations that tie into the next bar, instead of stabs on every group.
voice keys epiano vol=0.75 pan=-0.25
# Pad: unchanged common-tone pedal.
voice pad strings vol=0.35 pan=0.3
# Bass: same instrument, now walking quarters. Shorter gate so the walk
# articulates like a played line rather than legato fusion bass.
voice bass ebass vol=0.95 gate=0.85
# Drums: ride added to carry the time, hat moves to a soft foot-pedal role,
# kick feathers the group starts, snare only comps.
voice ride ride vol=0.6
voice kick kick vol=0.7
voice snare snare vol=0.65
voice hat hat vol=0.35
voice crash crash vol=0.5

pattern A
# Keys comp. Bar 1 hits beat 1 short, then the upbeat of beat 3, then
# pushes the Bb chord an eighth early. Bar 2 lands a late hit on the
# upbeat of beat 5 inside the 3-group. Bar 3 anticipates bar 4. Bar 4
# pushes A7alt (G C# F Bb C) onto the upbeat of beat 4, an eighth ahead of
# the 3-group, and lets it ring into Dm11 at the loop point.
keys | F3+C4+E4+G4+A4- .- . F3+C4+E4+G4+A4-- .--- . A3+D4+E4+G4 | -- .- A3+D4+E4+G4 . .- . A3+D4+E4+G4--- . | Bb3+D4+F4+A4--- .- Bb3+D4+F4+A4- . Bb3+D4+F4+A4-- . Bb3+D4+F4+A4 | - .-- Bb3+D4+F4+A4- . G3+C#4+F4+Bb4+C5!------ |
# Pad: unchanged.
pad  | E5+A5------------- | -------------- | -------------- | -------- F5+Bb5----- |
# Bass: seven walking quarters per bar. Group starts (beats 1, 3, 5) land on
# chord tones so the 2+2+3 shape is audible in the line, and the last
# quarter of each bar is a half-step approach to the next root (A1 to Bb1,
# Ab1 to G1, F#1 to G1, Eb2 to D2 at the loop point).
bass | D2- A2- C3- A2- D2- F2- A1- | Bb1- F2- A2- E2- Bb1- D2- Ab1- | G2- F2- D2- Bb1- A1- Bb1- F#1- | G1- Bb1- D2- F2- A1-! C#2- Eb2- |
# Ride: spang-a-lang adapted to 2+2+3. Each 2-group is beat, beat, swung
# upbeat; the 3-group is beat, beat, beat plus upbeat, accented at each
# group start. Bar 4 accents the A7alt push on the upbeat of beat 4.
ride  | X.xx X.xx X.x.xx | % | % | X.xx X..X ..x.xx |
# Hat foot on the second beat of each group (beats 2, 4, 6).
hat   | ..x. ..x. ..x... | % | % | % |
# Kick feathers the group starts softly, and drops a bomb under the A7alt
# push in bar 4.
kick  | o... o... o..... | % | % | o... o..X ...... |
# Snare: sparse ghosted comping on swung upbeats, different each bar, with a
# setup into the loop point.
snare | .... ...o ...o.. | .... .o.. ...o.o | ...o .... .o.... | .... ...x .o.o.x |
crash | x... .... ...... | _ | _ | _ |

loop A
